{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Moses hid his face</b> — Two times in the Masorah: here and the other: ויסתר עמל מעיני (and trouble would be hidden from my eyes). For had he gazed at the radiance of the Shekhinah within the bush and sought mercy for Israel, they would never have been exiled again, for the bush is a sign of עמו אנכי בצרה (I am with him in distress), and this is ויסתר עמל מעיני — for had he not hidden his face, he would have hidden trouble from his eyes."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:45.089688339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}